// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 8 „Teenused ja asjaajamine” (a2-036…040), level A2. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline, one year before the B1
// course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia (27) has lived in Tallinn for two months (a room at Malle Pärn's in Mustamäe,
// Keelekool Sõna in the mornings) and has errands to run: a bank account, an ID card, a local SIM card, a library card
// and the hairdresser before her first job interview. Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner books a
// service by phone (time, price, what to bring) and writes a message confirming it (039 Kasuta, final project).
// New minor characters: bank consultant Kristi Lepik (Linna Pank, Akadeemia tee 12) and her colleague Ivo, clerk Heli
// at the service office (teenindus), the door guard, librarian Marju (Malle works at the same library two days a
// week, module 4), the phone shop „Kõne” (customer service Kätlin, technician Ott), Aivar from the post office,
// hairdresser Kerttu (salong „Lõige”).
//   036 booking and changing a time — Soovin aega…, Kas … sobib?, Kas on võimalik varem / hiljem?, Kinnitan; days and
//       times in forms (kolmapäeval, pärast kella kahte); the bank appointment, moved because of a mock exam.
//   037 rules at the service office (ID card) — pean + ma-infinitive, saan / võin / ei tohi + da-infinitive, and the
//       impersonal present for recognition and simple use: siin müüakse, teenindus avatakse kell 9, kviitung
//       saadetakse e-postiga, siin ei suitsetata (A2 grammar plan: 08 impersonal present). Kasuta: rules for the new
//       lounge of the language school.
//   038 forms and instructions — the teie-imperative (täitke, kirjutage, valige, märkige, andke, näidake), the
//       library card, the SIM card contract, the bank form and a business card; impersonal again (kaart tehakse
//       kohe, arve saadetakse e-postiga, sularaha ei võeta).
//   039 the phone and customer service — Mis küsimuses te helistate?, Palun oodake, Ma ühendan teid…, Palun
//       korrake, tähthaaval; voice messages; impersonal again (kõnesid salvestatakse, teile helistatakse tagasi,
//       salong avatakse kell 10); final project: booking a service by phone and a confirming message.
// Recycling of module 7 (pood, raha ja ostud): hind, euro, maksma, kaardiga, sularaha, kviitung, tagastama,
// soodustus, odav, kallis / kallim, tasuta, kassa, ostma. Harno A2 formats trained: listening with short answers
// (played twice) and dialogue T/F, voice messages with „what happens next”, set phrases MC, signs matched, a
// ~130-word text, a letter with 3-option gaps, a message ≥ 30 words, business card into text, picture description,
// question cards in pairs. Lesson 5 is the module's check (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/a2/module08.js.
